# =============================================================================
# 99 — Teardown (stop ALL billing)
# =============================================================================
#
# ⚠️  LEARNING REFERENCE — read it, run it yourself when ready.
# ⚠️  DESTRUCTIVE — deleting the resource group deletes EVERYTHING inside it,
#     irreversibly. That's exactly what you want when done learning/demoing,
#     but make sure nothing else you care about lives in this RG first.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THEORY — Why "delete the resource group" is the whole cost-safety story
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything in 00-09 was created inside ONE resource group ($RG). Deleting that
# group deletes every resource in it in one operation, and billing for all of
# them stops immediately. This is why putting a whole learning project in a
# single dedicated RG matters: there's exactly one thing to remember to remove,
# and no risk of a forgotten Redis cache (the only non-free item) quietly
# draining your credit for weeks.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

RG="rg-highfidelity-learning"

# See what will be destroyed BEFORE doing it:
az resource list --resource-group "$RG" --output table

# Delete the whole group. --no-wait returns immediately; deletion continues in
# the background (can take several minutes). Drop --no-wait to block until done.
az group delete \
  --name "$RG" \
  --yes \
  --no-wait

# Confirm it's gone (once background deletion finishes this returns false):
az group exists --name "$RG"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you only want to remove the ONE expensive resource (Redis) but keep the
# rest of the free-tier stack running:
#   az redis delete --name "redis-highfid-$SUFFIX" --resource-group "$RG" --yes
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
